   - `E_NOT_FOUND` is message-specific and non-retryable; keep messages limited to the resource kind plus the caller's own request identifier, never an identifier discovered from another tenant.
   - Normalize resource kind and caller identifier at the constructor boundary so HTTP handlers and stores do not each invent their own not-found message shape.
